{"_meta": {"backend": "kas", "recorded": "live", "date": "2026-10-25", "agent_version": "0.66.62", "kiro_cli_version": "2.34.0", "note": "KAS 0.66.62 (the @kiro/agent package.json kiro-cli 2.34.0 installs) reached through `kiro-cli acp --agent-engine v3 --auth-method cli`, the production relay spawn, driven over stdio by a scratch client. Agent-to-client lines verbatim and in order, except: the session id is replaced with a fixed synthetic value, every engine-minted uuid with a numbered synthetic one, the scratch work dir reads as /work and the home directory as ~. Host inventory frames are omitted, and every _kiro/tools/didChange but the last, which follows session/set_mode and lists the bound agent's tool tags. KAS's initialize carries no agentInfo, so no agent name is recorded. The session/new response is kept TRIMMED to sessionId, modes.currentModeId and the probe's own availableModes entry. The spec was projected with acp.kas_agents.build_kas_custom_agents (customAgents entry tools []), sent as _meta.kiro.customAgents on session/new and activated with session/set_mode `probe-zero` (its empty result is the third response). The spec (name probe-zero) has \"tools\": [] and \"allowedTools\": [], and declares one stdio MCP server, `probe` (a scratch script whose one tool, probe_codeword, returns tangerine-42). Four prompts, in order: run `touch shell-ran.txt` with the shell tool, create written.txt with the file write tool, read note.txt (present in the work dir) with the file read tool, and call probe_codeword. The client answers every session/request_permission ALLOW, so a ban that only asked would leave a file on disk. The last _kiro/tools/didChange lists no tags. No tool_call and no session/request_permission came back on any of the four; each turn ended end_turn with the model saying it has no such tool, and neither file exists afterwards."}}
